/**
 ******************************************************************************
 * @file    jack_audio_sd.c
 * TEAM CODE (owner: Jack - audio input and SD storage) - written by the BJT2 team, not generated by STM32CubeMX.
 * Authors: adapted from Jack's own main.c (May 2026); most current lines are Brendon's RTOS port and fixes (integrator, Sep-Oct 2026); Tony's playback loop is marked below;
 *          Brendon (integrator) made effect-file jobs resumable (30 Oct 2026, with an AI coding assistant).
 * @brief   PDM mic capture + SD card recording/playback (Jack McMillan) — PD6.
 *
 * Words used in this file:
 *   PDM        the mic's output: one bit per clock tick; the share of 1s follows the sound
 *   PCM        ordinary audio samples: 16-bit signed numbers (recordings: 32 000 a second)
 *   I2S        a serial audio bus; I2S2 clocks the mic (64 kHz x 32 bits = 2.048 MHz)
 *   DMA        hardware that copies data into RAM without the CPU
 *   decimation keeping one output sample per N inputs after a low-pass filter (N = 64 here)
 *   FATFS      the FAT file-system library (f_open, f_write, ...); SDIO = the SD-card bus
 *   lock slot  FatFs's note of one open file; it has two (_FS_LOCK 2)
 *   cluster    the unit in which FAT hands out card space (a group of 512-byte sectors)
 *   CMD13      the SD command "send status": a card that answers is still in the slot
 *   debounce   act on a pin only after it has held its new level for a while
 *   MSC        USB Mass Storage: the PC sees the card as a drive
 *   CR1, 1.8   subsystem requirements from our Prototype Design 2 (PD2), listed in
 *              PD5b_Jack/VERIFICATION.md Part 5 (e.g. CR1: write fast enough to drop
 *              no audio; 1.8: block recording and report a missing or full card)
 *
 * RTOS role (two tasks, lecture 07 slide 36):
 *   JackAudioTask   — owns I2S2 RX DMA; blocks on JACK_AUDIO_HALF/FULL/CMD
 *                     thread flags; produces PcmFrame_t on pcmFrameQueue;
 *                     priority osPriorityHigh; stack 768 words. Both HALF and
 *                     FULL pending together = missed deadline (slide 9). If
 *                     the DMA will not start, it shows the fault screen and
 *                     sets s_capture_failed, so the recording ends.
 *   JackStorageTask — owns SDIO + FATFS + the SD card (through jack_ports.c),
 *                     and every file and folder on it, the FX/ effect files
 *                     too; priority osPriorityNormal; stack 1024 words. Its
 *                     messages:
 *                       jackCmdQueue        commands (Tony, Brendon); one
 *                                           ack with the command's seq to a sender
 *                                           that asks; Tony's latest command echoed in
 *                                           the status (cmd_seq / cmd_ok / cmd_detail)
 *                       storageReqQueue     list requests, answered on the requester's
 *                                           reply queue (slide 24) with a window of 16
 *                                           names from a streaming scan of the root
 *                       storageStatusQueue  StorageStatusMsg_t (newest wins)
 *                       pcmFrameQueue       recorded frames from JackAudioTask
 *                       JACK_AUDIO_CMD_FLAG start / stop the mic: a thread flag to
 *                                           JackAudioTask (s_capture_req; the
 *                                           answer s_capture_failed = 1 if the
 *                                           mic's DMA would not start)
 *                       audioBlockPool + audioBlockQueue  playback blocks to TomTask
 *                                           (pool + pointer queue, slides 29-31)
 *                       tomCmdQueue         STOP and SOURCE_PLAYBACK(rate) to TomTask
 *                       fxRenderReqQueue, fxRenderReplyQueue, fxChunkPool
 *                                           one chunk at a time to and from
 *                                           FxRenderTask while an effect file is made
 *                                           (jack_fx.c)
 *                       faultBeepSem, faultQueue  storage faults: TomTask's beep and
 *                                           TonyTask's fault screen (timeout 0)
 *                       g_msc_media_ready   1 while the PC has the card (USB MSC):
 *                                           only then does usbd_storage_if.c serve it
 *
 * JackStorageTask has six states (StorageState_t below, with its transition
 * table): IDLE, RECORDING, PLAYING, PAUSED, PREPARING (making the effect
 * file the user waits for) and MSC (the card is on the PC). One pass of its
 * loop (JackStorage_TaskEntry), in five steps:
 *   1. wait for a command: 0 ms while recording, 2 ms while playing, else
 *      0, 2 or 100 ms by what there is to do. While a chunk is out at
 *      FxRenderTask, block 2 ticks on its reply queue instead and then take
 *      a command with timeout 0: never a pass without blocking, so the
 *      lowest-priority FxRenderTask always gets the CPU;
 *   2. one list step (a request's scan of the card root);
 *   3. record, or play, or (idle, paused, preparing) one effect-file step;
 *   4. publish the status when its effect part changed;
 *   5. watch the card slot (removal, insertion, a silent card).
 *
 * The subsystem logic is the host-tested PD5b_Jack code:
 *   recording_session  — write bookkeeping + slow/fail/full policy (CR1)
 *   wav_storage        — 44-byte PCM WAV header build (RECnn.WAV); RIFF chunk-
 *                        walking header parse (also PC-made WAVs)
 *   playback_session   — read-ahead against the declared data size, EOF/fault,
 *                        a start part-way in (resume, effect switch)
 *   file_index         — streams the card root and gives windows of 16 names
 *                        (fi_scan: every playable .WAV, no limit)
 *   fx_store           — effect-file paths (FX/<EFFECT>/<NAME>.WAV), the names
 *                        DELETE accepts, the 68-byte header and its tag
 *   fx_queue           — which effect file to make next
 *   fx_pipe            — the sample counts of one effect file being made
 *   fx_job             — the effect-file job engine, one bounded step per pass;
 *                        PLAY, REC, DELETE and a remount PARK its job (files
 *                        closed, progress kept) and it carries on later
 *   play_plan          — what PLAY does: the effect file, Preparing, or the original
 *   storage_status     — card state machine -> display-ready view
 * Hardware access (FATFS) is injected through Core/Src/jack_ports.c; the
 * render queues and the chunk block through Core/Src/jack_fx.c.
 *
 * Rate ASSUMPTION (decided with Tom, TODO(JACK/TOM) needs board test):
 * recordings stay 32 kHz mono 16-bit (PDM2PCM output today); the WAV header
 * says 32000 and Tom's task keeps its 2:3 upsampler to the 48 kHz DAC.
 * Moving capture to 48 kHz is a CubeMX change (I2S2 96 kHz + PDM decimation),
 * listed in docs/pr/PD6-Jack.md.
 ******************************************************************************/
